+Raw `ToolDefinition` outputs may add a pure synchronous `output.validate(value)` that returns bounded, non-sensitive violations for constraints beyond `output.schema`. The registry checks every successful body, wrapper, or post-policy value after freezing and before rendering, including nested calls. A violation produces `INVALID_TOOL_OUTPUT`; thrown exceptions expose only `output.validate failed`. Additional validators do not change generated SDK types. See the [output declaration](../../../docs/subsystems/tools.md#tooldefinition--a-registered-tool) for registration ownership and admission semantics.
 
